> how do you playback a ttyrec type file (bz2) under windows xp?  searching
> isnt helping...

If the bz2 is you problem, just run "bzip2 -d" on it. (The suffix means
that the file is compressed, and your tty player might need you to
uncompress it.)

If you need a tty player for Windows, IPBT compiles cleanly under Cygwin:
http://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/ipbt/ .

